                                      1 ; Read-back logger + experiment switches, interrupt part. Lives in bank07 free space (zero padding from D9F5).
                                      2 ; The INT0 dispatcher (CODE:4D12, register bank 2, saves ACC/B/DPTR/PSW) calls its four bank07 sub-handlers through
                                      3 ; stubs CODE:1ACE/1AD4/1ADA/1AE0 (90 hi lo 02 02AE). The stubs now point at the jump table below; each wrapper logs
                                      4 ; one record and then jumps to the original handler:
                                      5 ;   ev1 bit4 -> B26E (TV-out vsync)   ev2 bit1 -> B222 (capture done)   ev3 bit14 -> 9E43   ev4 bit2 -> B6E8 (JPEG done)
                                      6 ;   ev5 = JPEG start for video recording: bank07:AB1E (output address [5676] -> 7324, source descriptor 1E75 via A943,
                                      7 ;         start bit 7300.2 via 82DA), entered only by LJMP from the JPEG scheduler at 96A9
                                      8 ;   ev6 = capture-done for a field the gate rejects (not passed to B222)
                                      9 ; Delays (x256 DJNZ loops, 0 = none; tearing experiments): [6BEB] before B222 (accepted capture-done, before the
                                     10 ;   buffer swap), [6BEE] before the JPEG start (ev5), [6BEF] at a rejected field's capture-done.
                                     11 ;   [6BEE] = FF: instead wait until the capture has finished the current field (720D bit2 set), max 255x256 polls.
                                     12 ; Edge fix [6BFB] (bit0 = top, bit1 = bottom; 0 = off): right before the JPEG start bit is set (82DA, called from the two
                                     13 ;   D1 start paths AB72 / AC8F), copy field row 1 over row 0 (top field: WSS data line) and row 286 over row 287 (last
                                     14 ;   line: PAL half line / blanking) in BOTH capture buffers (table 16FC, 20-byte entries, address in bytes 1-3 of
                                     15 ;   entries 0 and 1; line pitch 1440 bytes). In D1 the JPEG engine reads the capture buffer directly (lock-step);
                                     16 ;   [5676] at this point is the bitstream OUTPUT address (7324/7410), not the picture. The buffer about to be encoded is
                                     17 ;   complete (JPEG start waits for end of field); the other one is fixed again before its own encode.
                                     18 ;   The AC8F path is logged as event 3 (bit14 never fires). It starts mid-field: with [6BFC] = FF it first waits for
                                     19 ;   the end of the field too (as ev5 does with [6BEE] = FF), so the edge fix sees complete rows 286/287.
                                     20 ; Field gate (50i experiments): the dispatcher's own "720D.0 = 1" test (CODE:4DB7) is NOPed; ev2 decides by [6BEC]:
                                     21 ;   0 = stock (field with 720D.0 = 1 only), 1 = both fields, 2 = field with 720D.0 = 0 only.
                                     22 ; Per-frame pokes: UPOKE.BIN entries with flags bit3 ("frame") are applied on every accepted capture-done, before B222.
                                     23 ;
                                     24 ; Logging is armed by the record-start hook (poke_b13.asm, loginit) and writes into the JUNK chunk of the AVI header
                                     25 ; that the firmware builds in big memory at 0x7D0000 (window page 0xFA at XDATA 0x8000; flushed to the card at stop).
                                     26 ; Big-memory window: 7008/09 = read page, 700A/0B = write page.
                                     27 ; XDATA: 6BE0 = 0x5A armed, 6BE1/6BE2 = write ptr (XDATA address in the window), 6BE3 = record length,
                                     28 ; 6BE4 = sequence number, 6BE5-6BEA = call counters ev1-ev6 (always counted), 6BEB = delay before B222,
                                     29 ; 6BEC = field gate, 6BED = event mask (bit n = log event n; 0 = log all), 6BEE / 6BEF = delays (see above).
                                     30 ; All cleared at boot (poke_b10.asm).
                                     31 ; Record: A0+event, seq, TH0, TL0, TH2, TL2, then the bytes of every "peek" entry (flags & F4 == 34) in file order.
                                     32 ; Peek addresses must be below 0x8000 (0x8000-0xFFFF is the window, mapped to the log page while we read).
                                     33 
                                     34         .area   CODE (ABS)
      00DA00                         35         .org    0xDA00
                                     36 
      00DA00 02 DA 15         [24]   37         ljmp    ev1                 ; DA00 <- stub 1ACE
      00DA03 02 DB BC         [24]   38         ljmp    ev2                 ; DA03 <- stub 1AD4
      00DA06 02 DA 1E         [24]   39         ljmp    ev3                 ; DA06 <- stub 1ADA
      00DA09 02 DA 27         [24]   40         ljmp    ev4                 ; DA09 <- stub 1AE0
      00DA0C 02 DA 30         [24]   41         ljmp    ev5                 ; DA0C <- bank07:96A9 (LJMP AB1E)
      00DA0F 02 DA 6C         [24]   42         ljmp    efa                 ; DA0F <- bank07:AB72 (LCALL 82DA, start path AB1E)
      00DA12 02 DA 5C         [24]   43         ljmp    efb                 ; DA12 <- bank07:AC8F (LCALL 82DA, start path AC40)
                                     44 
      00DA15 75 F0 01         [24]   45 ev1:    mov     0xF0,#1
      00DA18 12 DC 44         [24]   46         lcall   log
      00DA1B 02 B2 6E         [24]   47         ljmp    0xB26E
